# TypeScript/JavaScript Security

> This file extends [common/security.mdc](../common/security.mdc) with TypeScript/JavaScript specific content.

## Secret Management

```typescript
// NEVER: Hardcoded secrets
const clickhousePassword = "secret-value"

// Gateway and producer read secrets from process env / secret storage, not
// from Vite-prefixed client variables.
```

Never place a secret in `VITE_*`; Vite exposes those values to the browser.
Parse `unknown` inputs with `zod/mini` before object spread, property access,
or protocol dispatch. Validate GraphQL pagination cursors, Redis Stream ids,
Dataset Events, and export ids at the boundary rather than trusting
browser-supplied identifiers.

Use the canonical `security-reviewer` agent for comprehensive audits when the
change warrants one.
